# Rule writing

**One home:** project rules live only under `.cursor/rules/`. Do not add a parallel root `rules/` or nest under `AppName/.cursor/rules/`.

**Two tiers:**
- `global/` — always-on or cross-app shared
- `<app-slug>/` — that app’s policy only (globs for that app)

**Write for any LLM:** plain language; one concern per file; keep short and actionable; concrete do/don’t; define or link standing terms (do not redefine); no chat-only knowledge — point at the owner doc.

**Frontmatter required:** `description` + either `alwaysApply: true` or `globs`.

**Same turn:** behaviour/handoff changes still update owner docs (`docs-first`, `session-independence`). Index: `.cursor/rules/README.md`.
